On Dec 14, 2007 9:06 PM, Penguino <spheniscine@gmail.com> wrote:
> However, (su'ore)me'i would not be the same as su'o(reme'i) .uinai

Besides that problem, which could be simply defined away by choosing
one interpretation as the correct one, my problem with that is that I
already have a different candidate interpretation for adjacent quantifiers.

I like to interpret for example {za'u re me'i xa} "more than two, less than
six" as "more than two and less than six", rather than as "more than
four" or as "less than four".

My interpretation was proposed here:
<http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=BPFK+Section%3A+Inexact+Numbers>

